IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `types`

§ `SCA-RTS Chapter III — Exemptions from strong customer authentication`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Commission Delegated Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Chapter III, Articles 10 to
-- 21, together with the ANNEX (OJ L 69, 13.3.2018, p. 43) on which Article 18
-- depends.  OJ L 69, 13.3.2018, p. 31.
--
-- This is the module that answers "is SCA required, or is an exemption
-- available". It is the commercially load-bearing part of the instrument.
--
-- Every Article here states a POWER, not a duty: "payment service providers
-- shall be allowed not to apply strong customer authentication". Each
-- predicate therefore answers "is the exemption AVAILABLE", never "is SCA
-- disapplied" -- the decision to take an available exemption stays with the
-- provider, and for a card transaction the issuer may decline an exemption
-- the acquirer requested. See NOTES.md section 5.
--
-- The two exceptions are Arts 13(1) and 14(1), which are DUTIES and are
-- encoded as such: they beat an otherwise available exemption on the same
-- transaction.
--
-- The Annex is encoded twice over -- forward (which band an amount falls in,
-- and what fraud rate that band demands) and inverted (given an acquirer's
-- fraud rate, the largest amount it may exempt). The inversion is what an
-- orchestrator needs at routing time.
--
-- Article 18 forward-references Article 20 for the cessation state. That is
-- deliberate: Art 20 is what actually decides whether a given provider may
-- use the Art 18 exemption today, and the Articles are kept in the
-- Regulation's own order rather than reordered to suit the dependency.
--
-- Source text: registers/source-bundle/reg-del-2018-389.txt
-- ===========================================================================

§§ `Article 10 — Payment account information`

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 10(2)(b)"
`article 10 lookback days` MEANS 90

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 10(1)(b)"
`article 10 transaction history window days` MEANS 90

-- Art 10(1): available where the user is limited to the balance and/or the
-- transactions of the last 90 days, online, without disclosure of sensitive
-- payment data, and subject to Article 2.
-- Art 10(2): NOT available where (a) it is the first online access, or (b)
-- more than 90 days have elapsed since the last SCA-authenticated access.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 10"
GIVEN a IS AN `Account Information Access`
    , `article 2 monitoring is in place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `article 10 exemption is available` IF
        `article 2 monitoring is in place`
    AND a's `access is limited to the balance or the last 90 days of transactions`
    AND NOT a's `sensitive payment data is disclosed`
    AND NOT a's `this is the first online access to that information`
    AND a's `days elapsed since that information was last accessed with SCA applied`
            AT MOST `article 10 lookback days`


§§ `Article 11 — Contactless payments at point of sale`

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 11(a)"
`article 11 individual amount ceiling in euro` MEANS 50

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 11(b)"
`article 11 cumulative amount ceiling in euro` MEANS 150

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 11(c)"
`article 11 consecutive transaction ceiling` MEANS 5

-- READING TAKEN (register entry AR-01): the Regulation writes
--   "(a) ... does not exceed EUR 50; and (b) ... does not exceed EUR 150;
--    or (c) ... does not exceed five."
-- read here as  (a) AND ( (b) OR (c) ) — the individual ceiling is always
-- required and the provider may run either counter. The competing reading,
-- ( (a) AND (b) ) OR (c), would let a EUR 900 contactless tap ride the count
-- limb with no amount cap at all, which Art 11's heading and recital 9 do
-- not support.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 11"
GIVEN t IS A `Payment Transaction`
    , c IS AN `Exemption Counters`
    , `article 2 monitoring is in place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `article 11 exemption is available` IF
        `article 2 monitoring is in place`
    AND t's `initiation channel` EQUALS `contactless at point of sale`
    AND t's `amount in euro` AT MOST `article 11 individual amount ceiling in euro`
    AND (    c's `cumulative amount in euro of previous transactions since SCA was last applied`
                 AT MOST `article 11 cumulative amount ceiling in euro`
          OR c's `number of previous transactions since SCA was last applied`
                 AT MOST `article 11 consecutive transaction ceiling` )


§§ `Article 12 — Unattended terminals for transport fares and parking fees`

-- Art 12 carries NO amount ceiling and NO counter. The only conditions are
-- the unattended terminal, the transport-fare-or-parking-fee purpose, and
-- Article 2 compliance.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 12"
GIVEN t IS A `Payment Transaction`
    , `article 2 monitoring is in place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `article 12 exemption is available` IF
        `article 2 monitoring is in place`
    AND t's `initiation channel` EQUALS `unattended terminal`
    AND t's `purpose is a transport fare or a parking fee`


§§ `Article 13 — Trusted beneficiaries`

-- Art 13(1) is a DUTY, not an exemption: SCA SHALL be applied where the payer
-- creates or amends the list.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 13(1)"
GIVEN t IS A `Payment Transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `article 13(1) requires strong customer authentication` IF
    t's `creates or amends a list of trusted beneficiaries`

-- Art 13(2) is the exemption, conditioned on "the general authentication
-- requirements" — Article 2 — rather than on a cross-reference to Art 2 by
-- number. Treated as the same condition; see AR-02.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 13(2)"
GIVEN t IS A `Payment Transaction`
    , `article 2 monitoring is in place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `article 13 exemption is available` IF
        `article 2 monitoring is in place`
    AND t's `payee is on a list of trusted beneficiaries previously created by the payer`
    AND NOT t's `creates or amends a list of trusted beneficiaries`


§§ `Article 14 — Recurring transactions`

-- Art 14(1) is a DUTY: SCA SHALL be applied when the payer creates, amends,
-- or initiates for the first time a series of recurring transactions WITH THE
-- SAME AMOUNT and WITH THE SAME PAYEE.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 14(1)"
GIVEN t IS A `Payment Transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `article 14(1) requires strong customer authentication` IF
    t's `creates amends or first initiates a recurring series`

-- Art 14(2): the exemption reaches only the SUBSEQUENT transactions in that
-- series. A varying amount takes the series outside Art 14 entirely; see
-- AR-05, which matters for travel instalment plans priced in a currency other
-- than the billing currency.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 14(2)"
GIVEN t IS A `Payment Transaction`
    , `article 2 monitoring is in place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `article 14 exemption is available` IF
        `article 2 monitoring is in place`
    AND t's `is a subsequent transaction in a series of the same amount to the same payee`
    AND NOT t's `creates amends or first initiates a recurring series`


§§ `Article 15 — Credit transfers between accounts held by the same person`

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 15"
GIVEN t IS A `Payment Transaction`
    , `article 2 monitoring is in place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `article 15 exemption is available` IF
        `article 2 monitoring is in place`
    AND t's `transaction type` EQUALS `credit transfer`
    AND t's `payer and payee are the same natural or legal person`
    AND t's `both payment accounts held by the same account servicing PSP`


§§ `Article 16 — Low-value transactions`

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 16(a)"
`article 16 individual amount ceiling in euro` MEANS 30

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 16(b)"
`article 16 cumulative amount ceiling in euro` MEANS 100

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 16(c)"
`article 16 consecutive transaction ceiling` MEANS 5

-- Same "(a) and (b); or (c)" drafting as Art 11, read the same way: AR-01.
-- Note that Art 16, unlike Arts 10 to 12 and 15, is NOT expressed as subject
-- to Article 2. That silence is preserved here rather than repaired: see
-- AR-02.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 16"
GIVEN t IS A `Payment Transaction`
    , c IS AN `Exemption Counters`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `article 16 exemption is available` IF
        t's `initiation channel` EQUALS `remote electronic`
    AND t's `amount in euro` AT MOST `article 16 individual amount ceiling in euro`
    AND (    c's `cumulative amount in euro of previous transactions since SCA was last applied`
                 AT MOST `article 16 cumulative amount ceiling in euro`
          OR c's `number of previous transactions since SCA was last applied`
                 AT MOST `article 16 consecutive transaction ceiling` )


§§ `Article 17 — Secure corporate payment processes and protocols`

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 17"
GIVEN t IS A `Payment Transaction`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `article 17 exemption is available` IF
        t's `payer kind` EQUALS `legal person who is not a consumer`
    AND t's `initiated through a dedicated corporate payment process or protocol`
    AND t's `that process is made available only to payers who are not consumers`
    AND t's `competent authorities are satisfied with that process`


§§ `Annex — Exemption threshold values and reference fraud rates`

-- ANNEX (OJ L 69, 13.3.2018, p. 43)
--
--   ETV        remote electronic         remote electronic
--              card-based payments       credit transfers
--   EUR 500    0,01 %                    0,005 %
--   EUR 250    0,06 %                    0,01 %
--   EUR 100    0,13 %                    0,015 %
--
-- The table reads downwards from the tightest fraud requirement: to exempt a
-- transaction up to EUR 500 the provider needs a fraud rate at or below
-- 0.01 % on cards; the same provider at 0.13 % may still exempt up to EUR 100.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Annex"
`article 18 exemption threshold values in euro` MEANS LIST 100, 250, 500

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Annex"
`highest exemption threshold value in euro` MEANS 500

-- The band a given amount falls into. Above EUR 500 there is no band, and
-- Article 18 is unavailable at any fraud rate; 0 is the "no band" marker and
-- is never a real ETV, since the Annex's lowest is EUR 100.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 18(2)(b) and Annex"
GIVEN `amount in euro` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`applicable exemption threshold value in euro` MEANS
    IF   `amount in euro` AT MOST 100
    THEN 100
    ELSE IF   `amount in euro` AT MOST 250
         THEN 250
         ELSE IF   `amount in euro` AT MOST 500
              THEN 500
              ELSE 0

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Annex"
GIVEN `transaction type` IS A `Transaction Type`
    , `exemption threshold value in euro` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reference fraud rate pct` MEANS
    CONSIDER `transaction type`
    WHEN `card based payment` THEN
        IF   `exemption threshold value in euro` EQUALS 500
        THEN 0.01
        ELSE IF   `exemption threshold value in euro` EQUALS 250
             THEN 0.06
             ELSE IF   `exemption threshold value in euro` EQUALS 100
                  THEN 0.13
                  ELSE 0
    WHEN `credit transfer` THEN
        IF   `exemption threshold value in euro` EQUALS 500
        THEN 0.005
        ELSE IF   `exemption threshold value in euro` EQUALS 250
             THEN 0.01
             ELSE IF   `exemption threshold value in euro` EQUALS 100
                  THEN 0.015
                  ELSE 0
    WHEN `other payment transaction` THEN 0

-- The Annex has exactly two rows. A transaction of any other type has no
-- reference fraud rate, so Art 18(2)(a) can never be satisfied for it.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Annex"
GIVEN `transaction type` IS A `Transaction Type`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the annex prices this transaction type` IF
        `transaction type` EQUALS `card based payment`
    OR  `transaction type` EQUALS `credit transfer`

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Annex"
GIVEN `transaction type` IS A `Transaction Type`
    , f IS A `Fraud Rate Report`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`monitored fraud rate pct` MEANS
    CONSIDER `transaction type`
    WHEN `card based payment`        THEN f's `remote card based payment fraud rate pct`
    WHEN `credit transfer`           THEN f's `remote credit transfer fraud rate pct`
    WHEN `other payment transaction` THEN 100


§§ `Article 18 — Transaction risk analysis`

-- Art 18(2)(c): the exemption fails if the real-time analysis identified ANY
-- of the six listed signals.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 18(2)(c)"
GIVEN r IS A `Real Time Risk Analysis`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the real time risk analysis identified no listed signal` IF
        NOT r's `abnormal spending or behavioural pattern of the payer`
    AND NOT r's `unusual information about the device or software access of the payer`
    AND NOT r's `malware infection in any session of the authentication procedure`
    AND NOT r's `known fraud scenario in the provision of payment services`
    AND NOT r's `abnormal location of the payer`
    AND NOT r's `high risk location of the payee`

-- Art 18(1) and (2): all three conditions, plus the Art 2 / 18(2)(c)
-- monitoring mechanisms the paragraph expressly relies on, plus the Art 20
-- cessation state, which is what actually decides whether this provider may
-- use the exemption at all today.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 18"
GIVEN t IS A `Payment Transaction`
    , r IS A `Real Time Risk Analysis`
    , p IS A `PSP Profile`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `article 18 exemption is available` IF
        p's `has transaction monitoring mechanisms under article 2`
    AND t's `initiation channel` EQUALS `remote electronic`
    AND `the annex prices this transaction type` (t's `transaction type`)
    AND `the article 18 exemption is not in cessation` p
    AND t's `amount in euro` AT MOST `highest exemption threshold value in euro`
    AND `monitored fraud rate pct` (t's `transaction type`) (p's `fraud rates`)
            AT MOST `reference fraud rate pct` (t's `transaction type`) band
    AND `the real time risk analysis identified no listed signal` r
    WHERE
        band MEANS `applicable exemption threshold value in euro` (t's `amount in euro`)

-- The highest amount this provider may exempt under Art 18 for a given
-- transaction type: the largest Annex band whose reference rate its monitored
-- fraud rate still meets. 0 means no band is open to it.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 18(2) and Annex"
GIVEN `transaction type` IS A `Transaction Type`
    , p IS A `PSP Profile`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`highest amount exemptible under article 18 in euro` MEANS
    IF   NOT `the annex prices this transaction type` `transaction type`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF   rate AT MOST (`reference fraud rate pct` `transaction type` 500)
         THEN 500
         ELSE IF   rate AT MOST (`reference fraud rate pct` `transaction type` 250)
              THEN 250
              ELSE IF   rate AT MOST (`reference fraud rate pct` `transaction type` 100)
                   THEN 100
                   ELSE 0
    WHERE
        rate MEANS `monitored fraud rate pct` `transaction type` (p's `fraud rates`)


§§ `Article 19 — Calculation of fraud rates`

-- Art 19(1) second subparagraph: the overall fraud rate is the total VALUE of
-- unauthorised or fraudulent remote transactions, whether or not the funds
-- were recovered, divided by the total value of all remote transactions of
-- that type, on a rolling quarterly basis (90 days).
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 19(1)"
`fraud rate rolling window days` MEANS 90

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 19(1)"
GIVEN `total value of unauthorised or fraudulent remote transactions` IS A NUMBER
    , `total value of all remote transactions of that type`            IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`overall fraud rate pct` MEANS
    IF   `total value of all remote transactions of that type` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE 100 TIMES (   `total value of unauthorised or fraudulent remote transactions`
                DIVIDED BY `total value of all remote transactions of that type` )


§§ `Article 20 — Cessation of exemptions based on transaction risk analysis`

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 20(2)"
`consecutive quarters above reference rate that force cessation` MEANS 2

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 20(3)"
`quarters at or below reference rate required before re-use` MEANS 1

-- Art 20(1): an immediate report to the competent authorities the moment a
-- monitored rate exceeds the applicable reference rate — one quarter is
-- enough to trigger the report, two are needed for cessation.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 20(1)"
GIVEN `transaction type` IS A `Transaction Type`
    , `exemption threshold value in euro` IS A NUMBER
    , p IS A `PSP Profile`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an immediate report to the competent authorities is due` IF
    `monitored fraud rate pct` `transaction type` (p's `fraud rates`)
        GREATER THAN `reference fraud rate pct` `transaction type` `exemption threshold value in euro`

-- Art 20(2) and (3) combined: the exemption is closed to this provider while
-- it has been above for two consecutive quarters, and stays closed after a
-- cessation until one quarter at or below has been achieved AND — Art 20(4) —
-- the competent authorities have been notified.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 20(2)–(4)"
GIVEN p IS A `PSP Profile`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the article 18 exemption is not in cessation` IF
        f's `consecutive quarters above the reference rate`
            LESS THAN `consecutive quarters above reference rate that force cessation`
    AND (    NOT f's `exemption previously ceased under article 20`
          OR (    f's `quarters at or below the reference rate since cessation`
                      AT LEAST `quarters at or below reference rate required before re-use`
              AND f's `competent authorities notified of the intention to use the exemption again` ) )
    WHERE
        f MEANS p's `fraud rates`


§§ `Article 21 — Monitoring`

-- Art 21(1): to use ANY of the Arts 10 to 18 exemptions the provider must
-- record and monitor the listed data at least quarterly, broken down between
-- remote and non-remote transactions.
@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 21(1)"
`maximum months between exemption monitoring reports` MEANS 3

@ref "Regulation (EU) 2018/389, Art 21(1)"
GIVEN `fraud rate and totals recorded per transaction type`   IS A BOOLEAN
    , `average transaction value recorded per exemption`      IS A BOOLEAN
    , `number and percentage of transactions per exemption recorded` IS A BOOLEAN
    , `months since the last monitoring report`               IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the article 21 monitoring conditions are met` IF
        `fraud rate and totals recorded per transaction type`
    AND `average transaction value recorded per exemption`
    AND `number and percentage of transactions per exemption recorded`
    AND `months since the last monitoring report`
            AT MOST `maximum months between exemption monitoring reports`



